    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2058230138052239482",
      "url": "https://x.com/Ezekle1/status/2058230138052239482",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Ezekle1/status/2058230138052239482",
      "text": "This little boy saved up for months. What he did with $3 will break you open.\nHis name is Miko. He's 8 years old, lives in Cebu, Philippines, and every time his lola gave him five pesos for being good  he didn't spend it.\n\nHe hid it inside a folded piece of paper tucked under his mattress. Coin by coin. Week by week. He told no one what it was for.\n\nHis grandfather  Lolo Carding, 79 years old  hadn't eaten at a restaurant in over a decade. Not since Lola passed. \"Wala nang saysay,\" he would say quietly. No point anymore.\n\nOne Saturday morning, Miko walked into his lolo's room, held out a small crumpled envelope, and said: \"Lolo, I saved enough. I want to take you out to eat.\"\n\nInside the envelope: 170 pesos. Just over $3.\n\nHe had already chosen the place  a Korean barbecue restaurant two jeepney rides away that he'd seen his classmates talk about. He didn't know if $3 was enough. He just knew his lolo deserved a table with a fire in the middle of it.\n\nThe owner seated them at the best spot by the window. When he understood what was happening  this tiny boy, this old man, this crumpled envelope he quietly told the staff: cook everything, charge nothing extra.\n\nMiko carefully placed every peso on the table himself. He wanted to pay. He needed to pay.\n\nLolo Carding didn't say much. He just watched his grandson pile meat onto his plate, blow on each piece so it wouldn't be too hot, and beam across the table like he'd just given him the whole world.\n\nBecause he had.\n\nWhen someone later asked Miko why he saved so long for this, he shrugged and said: \"Lolo always eats alone. I don't want him to eat alone.\"\n\nThree dollars. Two plates of Korean barbecue. One little boy who understood something about love that most adults have forgotten.\n In your life, you shouldn't be eating alone !",
      "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
